/-!
# The semi-free resolution of the ground ring over the chains on the loops of a circle

Brown's twisted tensor product resolves the ground ring `R` over the chains `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` on the
Moore loops of a CW complex `B` by a semi-free module with one free generator for each cell,
attached along a cycle representing the attaching map of the cell. For the circle, with one
`0`-cell `e₀` at the base point and one `1`-cell `e₁` attached along a loop `γ` going once around,
this module is

`K = C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₁`,  `D e₀ = 0`,  `D e₁ = ([γ] - [1]) e₀`,

where `[γ]` is the point chain of the Moore loop `γ` and `[1]` the unit. As a row-finite twisting
cocycle on the generators `Unit ⊕ Unit`, with `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index `0` and
`e₁ = Sum.inr ()` of index `1`, this is `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`: the generator `e₁` is
attached (`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach`) along the cycle `([γ] - [1]) e₀` to the free
module on `e₀` with zero differential (`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_m_inr`). It is one-sided, so the
module is semi-free (`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_m_eq_zero_of_le`). The differential of a vector
`α e₀ + β e₁` is `dα ± β ([γ] - [1])` on `e₀` and `dβ` on `e₁`
(`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_differential_apply`). The cocycle is defined for every Moore loop of
every space.

The circle's cocycle is the case `n = 0`, `x = [γ] - [1]` of the cocycle
`TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R n x` of one `(n + 1)`-cell attached along an `n`-cycle `x` of
`C_*(Ω_b B; R)`, and its lemmas specialize those of the general cocycle
(`TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply`). The sphere uses the general cocycle with the
attaching cycle of its top cell.

The augmentation `ε : K → R` takes the augmentation of the coefficient of `e₀`
(`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation`). It is linear over the augmentation of the loop chain algebra
(`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation_smul`), vanishes on boundaries
(`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation_differential`, and
`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation_cycleCellCocycle_differential` for an attaching cycle of
augmentation zero) and takes the value `1` on the cycle `e₀`. For an attaching cycle `x` of
augmentation zero, `ε` is a quasi-isomorphism as soon as right multiplication by `x` is injective
on homology and every cycle of augmentation zero is, up to a boundary, a right multiple of `x` by a
cycle (`TauCeti.exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`).

The main result is that `ε` is a quasi-isomorphism onto `R` when `B` is aspherical with fundamental
group infinite cyclic generated by the class of `γ`, as for the circle: every cycle of `K` with
augmentation zero is a boundary
(`TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`). Over an
aspherical space the homology of `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` is the group ring `R[π₁(B, b)]`, concentrated in
degree zero, so the homology of `K` is that of the complex `R[π₁] → R[π₁]` given by right
multiplication by `g - 1`, where `g` is the class of `γ`. That map is injective since `g` has
infinite order, and its cokernel is `R` through the augmentation since `g` generates. The proof
checks the two conditions of the general criterion for `x = [γ] - [1]` on representatives,
using that a cycle of the loop chain algebra whose degree-zero truncation vanishes is a boundary
(`TauCeti.exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero`).

The loop `γ` in the attaching row cannot be dropped. With the zero cocycle on the same two
generators, `e₁` is a cycle of augmentation zero which is not a boundary, for every space and every
nontrivial ring `R` (`TauCeti.exists_notMem_range_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero`): that module
is the direct sum of two shifted copies of `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`, whose homology is not that of a
point.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R n x`: the twisting cocycle of one `(n + 1)`-cell attached along an
  `n`-cycle `x` to one `0`-cell.
* `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`: the twisting cocycle of one `1`-cell attached along `γ` to one
  `0`-cell.
* `TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation B b R`: the augmentation of its free module.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply`: the differential on `α e₀ + β e₁`.
* `TauCeti.exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`: the module
  of a cell attached along `x` resolves the ground ring when right multiplication by `x` behaves
  as for a sphere.
* `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_differential_apply`: the differential on `α e₀ + β e₁`.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`: over an
  aspherical space whose fundamental group is infinite cyclic, generated by the class of `γ`, the
  augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`: the
  case of the circle and its counterclockwise loop.
* `TauCeti.exists_notMem_range_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero`: the zero cocycle on the same
  generators does not resolve `R`.

## References

* E. H. Brown, *Twisted tensor products, I*, Ann. of Math. (2) 69 (1959), 223–246.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Floer homology with DG coefficients.
  Applications to cotangent bundles*, arXiv:2404.07953, §1.4.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Morse homology with differential graded
  coefficients*, Progress in Mathematics 360, Birkhäuser, 2025, Chapters 3--4.
-/

public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicTopology

open scoped Topology

universe u

namespace TauCeti

/-! ### The cocycle of a cell attached along a cycle -/

section CycleCell

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

/-- **The twisting cocycle of one `(n + 1)`-cell attached along an `n`-cycle.** On the
generators `Unit ⊕ Unit`, the `0`-cell `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index `0` has zero row, and the cell
`e₁ = Sum.inr ()` of index `n + 1` is attached (`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach`) along
the cycle `x e₀`, for an `n`-cycle `x` of the chains `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` on the Moore loops. For a
sphere and the cycle swept out by the boundary of its top cell, this is Brown's semi-free
resolution of `R` over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. -/
def cycleCellCocycle (n : ℕ) (x : loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (hx : x ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (-(n : ℤ)))
    (hdx : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R x = 0) :
    RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (Unit ⊕ Unit) (Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ 0) (fun _ ↦ (n : ℤ) + 1)) :=
  (0 : RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      Unit (fun _ ↦ 0)).attach
    (fun _ ↦ Finsupp.single () x)
    (fun _ y ↦ by
      cases y
      simpa [show (0 : ℤ) - (n + 1) + 1 = -n by ring] using hx)
    (fun _ ↦ by simp [hdx])

variable {R} {n : ℕ} {x : loopChainAlgebra B b R}
  (hx : x ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (-(n : ℤ)))
  (hdx : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R x = 0)

@[simp]
theorem cycleCellCocycle_m_inl : (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m (Sum.inl ()) = 0 := by
  simp [cycleCellCocycle]

/-- The row of `e₁` is `x e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cycleCellCocycle_m_inr :
    (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m (Sum.inr ()) = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) x := by
  rw [cycleCellCocycle, RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach_m_inr, Finsupp.mapDomain_single]

/-- The cocycle is one-sided, so its free module is semi-free
(`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.wellFounded_mem_support`). -/
theorem cycleCellCocycle_m_eq_zero_of_le {y z : Unit ⊕ Unit}
    (h : Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ (0 : ℤ)) (fun _ ↦ (n : ℤ) + 1) y ≤
      Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ (0 : ℤ)) (fun _ ↦ (n : ℤ) + 1) z) :
    (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m y z = 0 :=
  RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach_m_eq_zero_of_le _ _ _ (fun _ _ _ ↦ by simp)
    (fun _ _ h ↦ absurd h (by simp)) y z h

/-- The differential of the free module of `TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R n x` on `α e₀ + β e₁`: the
coefficient of `e₀` is `dα + κ(β) x`, with `κ` the Koszul sign twist, and the coefficient of `e₁`
is `dβ`. -/
theorem cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m u =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inl ())) +
          (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist
              1 (u (Sum.inr ())) * x) +
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ())
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inr ()))) := by
  have hu : u = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (u (Sum.inl ())) +
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (u (Sum.inr ())) := by
    ext i
    rcases i with ⟨⟩ | ⟨⟩ <;> simp
  conv_lhs => rw [hu]
  simp [rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_single_koszulTwist, Finsupp.single_add]
  abel

/-- The coefficient of `e₀` in the differential of `u` is `d(u e₀) + κ(u e₁) x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m u
          (Sum.inl ()) =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inl ())) +
        (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist
            1 (u (Sum.inr ())) * x := by
  simp [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply]

/-- The coefficient of `e₁` in the differential of `u` is `d(u e₁)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m u
          (Sum.inr ()) =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inr ())) := by
  simp [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply]

/-- The differential of `α e₀` is `(dα) e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inl (α : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) α) =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R α) := by
  simp [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply]

/-- The differential of `β e₁` is `κ(β) x e₀ + (dβ) e₁`, with `κ` the Koszul sign twist. -/
theorem cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inr (β : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) β) =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
          ((InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
              (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 β * x) +
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R β) := by
  simp [cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply]

end CycleCell

section Cocycle

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

/-- **The twisting cocycle of one `1`-cell attached along a loop.** On the generators
`Unit ⊕ Unit`, the `0`-cell `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index `0` has zero row, and the `1`-cell
`e₁ = Sum.inr ()` of index `1` is attached along the cycle `([γ] - [1]) e₀`: the difference of the
point chain of the Moore loop `γ` and the unit of `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. It is the cocycle
`TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R 0 ([γ] - [1])` of a cell attached along a `0`-cycle. For a circle and a
loop going once around, this is Brown's semi-free resolution of `R` over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. -/
def loopCellCocycle (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (Unit ⊕ Unit) (Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ 0) (fun _ ↦ 1)) :=
  cycleCellCocycle R 0 (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
      (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1)
    (by
      have hp : cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
          (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) ∈
            cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 := by
        simpa using cubicalChainLof_mem (MooreLoopSpace B b) R
          (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ))
      simpa using sub_mem hp (SetLike.one_mem_graded (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)))
    (by simp [(loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_one_eq_zero])

variable {R}

@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_m_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).m (Sum.inl ()) = 0 :=
  cycleCellCocycle_m_inl _ _

/-- The row of `e₁` is `([γ] - [1]) e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_m_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).m (Sum.inr ()) = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
      (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
        (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1) :=
  cycleCellCocycle_m_inr _ _

/-- The cocycle is one-sided, so its free module is semi-free
(`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.wellFounded_mem_support`). -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_m_eq_zero_of_le (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) {x y : Unit ⊕ Unit}
    (h : Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ (0 : ℤ)) (fun _ ↦ 1) x ≤ Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ (0 : ℤ)) (fun _ ↦ 1) y) :
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).m x y = 0 :=
  cycleCellCocycle_m_eq_zero_of_le _ _ h

/-- The differential of the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` on `α e₀ + β e₁`: the
coefficient of `e₀` is `dα + κ(β) ([γ] - [1])`, with `κ` the Koszul sign twist, and the coefficient
of `e₁` is `dβ`. -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_apply (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inl ())) +
          (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist
              1 (u (Sum.inr ())) *
            (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
              (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1)) +
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ())
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inr ()))) :=
  cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply _ _ u

/-- The coefficient of `e₀` in the differential of `u` is `d(u e₀) + κ(u e₁) ([γ] - [1])`, with
`κ` the Koszul sign twist. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u
          (Sum.inl ()) =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inl ())) +
        (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist
            1 (u (Sum.inr ())) *
          (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
            (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1) :=
  cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl _ _ u

/-- The coefficient of `e₁` in the differential of `u` is `d(u e₁)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u
          (Sum.inr ()) =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inr ())) :=
  cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr _ _ u

/-- The differential of `α e₀` is `(dα) e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (α : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) α) =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R α) :=
  cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inl _ _ α

/-- The differential of `β e₁` is `κ(β) ([γ] - [1]) e₀ + (dβ) e₁`, with `κ` the Koszul sign
twist. -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (β : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) β) =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
          ((InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
              (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 β *
            (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
              (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1)) +
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R β) :=
  cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inr _ _ β

variable (B b R) in
/-- The augmentation of the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`: the augmentation of the
coefficient of the generator `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index zero. -/
def loopCellAugmentation : (Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) →ₗ[R] R :=
  (loopChainAugmentation B b R).toAlgHom.toLinearMap ∘ₗ Finsupp.lapply (Sum.inl ())

theorem loopCellAugmentation_apply (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R u = loopChainAugmentation B b R (u (Sum.inl ())) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The augmentation is linear over the augmentation of the loop chain algebra. -/
theorem loopCellAugmentation_smul (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R (a • u) =
      loopChainAugmentation B b R a * loopCellAugmentation B b R u := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

/-- The augmentation takes the augmentation of a coefficient of `e₀`; in particular it takes the
value `1` on the cycle `e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_single_inl (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) a) = loopChainAugmentation B b R a := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

/-- The augmentation vanishes on the multiples of `e₁`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_single_inr (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) a) = 0 := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

variable (B b R) in
/-- The augmentation is surjective: it takes `r e₀` to `r`. -/
theorem loopCellAugmentation_surjective : Function.Surjective (loopCellAugmentation B b R) :=
  fun r ↦ ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ r), by simp⟩

/-- The generator `e₀` is a cycle. -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl_one (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) 1) = 0 := by
  rw [RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.differential_single_one _ (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R),
    loopCellCocycle_m_inl]

/-- When the attaching cycle has augmentation zero, as it does in positive dimension, the
augmentation of the free module of `TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R n x` vanishes on boundaries. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_cycleCellCocycle_differential {n : ℕ} {x : loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hx : x ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (-(n : ℤ)))
    (hdx : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R x = 0)
    (hεx : loopChainAugmentation B b R x = 0) (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R
        (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m u) = 0 := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply, hεx]

/-- The augmentation vanishes on boundaries. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_differential (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R
        (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u) =
      0 :=
  loopCellAugmentation_cycleCellCocycle_differential _ _ (by simp) u

variable (B b R) in
/-- **The loop in the attaching row cannot be dropped.** For every space and every nontrivial
ring `R`, the free module of the zero cocycle on the generators `Unit ⊕ Unit` has a cycle of
augmentation zero which is not a boundary, namely `e₁ = Sum.inr ()`. So its augmentation is not
a quasi-isomorphism onto `R`, unlike that of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` over a circle. -/
theorem exists_notMem_range_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero [Nontrivial R] :
    ∃ u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R,
      rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) 0 u = 0 ∧
        loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0 ∧
        u ∉ LinearMap.range (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) 0) := by
  refine ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) 1, ?_, loopCellAugmentation_single_inr 1, ?_⟩
  · simp [(loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_one_eq_zero]
  · rintro ⟨v, hv⟩
    -- The coefficient of `e₁` would be a boundary with augmentation `1`.
    have h := congrArg (fun w ↦ loopChainAugmentation B b R (w (Sum.inr ()))) hv
    simp only [rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero, Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap_apply,
      Finsupp.mapRange_apply, DGAlgAugmentation.map_d, Finsupp.single_eq_same, map_one] at h
    exact zero_ne_one h

end Cocycle

/-! ### The resolution of a cell attached along a cycle -/

section CycleCellResolution

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {n : ℕ}
  {x : loopChainAlgebra B b R} (hx : x ∈ cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (-(n : ℤ)))
  (hdx : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R x = 0)

/-- A cycle `α` of augmentation zero which is, up to a boundary, a right multiple `β x` of a cycle
`β` gives a boundary `α e₀` of the free module of `TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R n x`: if
`α = β x + d w`, then `α e₀` is the boundary of `w e₀ + κ(β) e₁`. -/
private theorem exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_single_inl {α β w : loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hβ : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R β = 0)
    (hα : β * x + cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R w = α) :
    ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m v =
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) α := by
  -- The Koszul twist `κ` anticommutes with the differential, so `κ(β)` is a cycle.
  have hdκβ : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R
      ((InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
        (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 β) = 0 := by
    rw [← neg_eq_zero, ← (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.koszulTwist_map, hβ,
      map_zero]
  refine ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) w + Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ())
    ((InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 β), ?_⟩
  simp [cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inr, InternalGrading.koszulTwist_koszulTwist, hdκβ,
    ← hα, add_comm]

/-- **The module of a cell attached along a cycle resolves the ground ring** when right
multiplication by the attaching cycle `x` behaves as for a sphere: a cycle `β` with `β x` a
boundary is a boundary, and every cycle of augmentation zero is the sum of a right multiple `β x`
of a cycle `β` and a boundary. Then every cycle of the free module of
`TauCeti.cycleCellCocycle R n x` whose augmentation vanishes is a boundary. Since the augmentation
vanishes on boundaries (`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation_cycleCellCocycle_differential`) and takes
the value `1` on the cycle `e₀`, it is a quasi-isomorphism onto `R`. -/
theorem exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    (hεx : loopChainAugmentation B b R x = 0)
    (hinj : ∀ β w : loopChainAlgebra B b R,
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R β = 0 →
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R w = β * x →
      ∃ γ, cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R γ = β)
    (hsurj : ∀ α : loopChainAlgebra B b R,
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R α = 0 →
      loopChainAugmentation B b R α = 0 → ∃ β w : loopChainAlgebra B b R,
        cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R β = 0 ∧
        β * x + cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R w = α)
    {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m u =
        0)
    (hε : loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0) :
    ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m v =
        u := by
  set D := rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
    (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).m with hD
  -- The Koszul twist `κ` anticommutes with the differential.
  have hdκ (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R
          ((InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
            (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 a) =
        -(InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
          (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1
            (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R a) := by
    rw [(loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).toIsNonUnitalDGAlgebra.koszulTwist_map, neg_neg]
  have hu0 := congrArg (· (Sum.inl ())) hu
  have hu1 := congrArg (· (Sum.inr ())) hu
  simp only [hD, cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl, cycleCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr,
    Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply] at hu0 hu1
  -- The coefficient `β` of `e₁` is a cycle with `κ(β) x` a boundary, so `κ(β) = dγ`.
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ⟩ := hinj _ (-u (Sum.inl ())) (by rw [hdκ, hu1, map_zero, neg_zero])
    (by rw [map_neg]; exact neg_eq_of_add_eq_zero_right hu0)
  -- Subtracting the boundary of `-κ(γ) e₁` leaves a cycle `w` supported on `e₀`.
  set w := u - D (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (-(InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
    (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 γ)) with hw
  have hw1 : w (Sum.inr ()) = 0 := by
    simp [hw, hD, cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inr, hdκ, hγ,
      InternalGrading.koszulTwist_koszulTwist]
  have hw' : w = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (w (Sum.inl ())) := by
    ext i
    rcases i with ⟨⟩ | ⟨⟩ <;> simp [hw1]
  have hdw : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (w (Sum.inl ())) = 0 := by
    have hDw : D w = 0 := by
      rw [hw, map_sub, hu, (cycleCellCocycle R n x hx hdx).differential_sq_zero
        (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R), sub_zero]
    have := congrArg (· (Sum.inl ())) hDw
    rw [hw', hD, cycleCellCocycle_differential_single_inl] at this
    simpa using this
  have hεw : loopChainAugmentation B b R (w (Sum.inl ())) = 0 := by
    rw [← loopCellAugmentation_apply, hw, map_sub, hε, hD,
      loopCellAugmentation_cycleCellCocycle_differential hx hdx hεx, sub_zero]
  -- The cycle `w e₀` of augmentation zero is a boundary.
  obtain ⟨β', w', hβ', hβw'⟩ := hsurj _ hdw hεw
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_single_inl hx hdx hβ' hβw'
  rw [← hD] at hv
  refine ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (-(InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
    (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 γ) + v, ?_⟩
  rw [map_add, hv, ← hw', hw]
  abel

end CycleCellResolution

section Resolution

variable {B : Type u} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- **Brown's resolution of the ground ring over the chains on the loops of a circle.** Let `B` be
aspherical at `b`, and let the class `g` of the Moore loop `γ` generate the fundamental group
`π₁(B, b)` and have infinite order, as for a loop going once around a circle. Then every cycle of
the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` whose augmentation vanishes is a boundary. Since
the augmentation vanishes on boundaries and takes the value `1` on the cycle `e₀`, it is a
quasi-isomorphism onto `R`: the module is a semi-free resolution of `R` over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b)) {γ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ))
    {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u = 0)
    (hε : loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0) :
    ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m v = u := by
  set T := loopChainToGroupAlgebra B b R
  set g := MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ
  set p := cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
    (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ))
  have hTp : T (p - 1) = MonoidAlgebra.single g 1 - 1 := by
    rw [map_sub, map_one, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_lof_zero, loopZeroChainToGroupAlgebra_ofCube,
      SingularCube.point_apply]
  refine exists_cycleCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero _ _ (by simp)
    (fun β w hβ hw ↦ ?_) (fun α hα hεα ↦ ?_) hu hε
  · -- The truncation `t` of a cycle `β` with `β ([γ] - [1]) = dw` satisfies `t (g - 1) = 0`, so
    -- `t = 0` and `β` is a boundary.
    refine exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB hβ ?_
    have h := congrArg T hw
    rw [loopChainToGroupAlgebra_differential, map_mul, hTp,
      ← zero_mul (MonoidAlgebra.single g 1 - 1)] at h
    exact (isRegular_single_sub_one_of_not_isOfFinOrder hinf).right h.symm
  · -- The truncation of a cycle `α` of augmentation zero is a left multiple of `g - 1`.
    have hker : T α ∈ RingHom.ker (MonoidAlgebra.augmentation R (FundamentalGroup B b)) := by
      rw [RingHom.mem_ker, augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra, hεα]
    rw [MonoidAlgebra.ker_augmentation_eq_span_of_closure_eq_top R
      (s := {g}) (by rw [← Subgroup.zpowers_eq_closure, hgen]), Set.image_singleton,
      Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at hker
    obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := hker
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := loopZeroChainToGroupAlgebra_surjective (R := R) (x := b) h
    -- Subtracting `δ ([γ] - [1])`, for a zero chain `δ` lifting the multiplier, leaves a cycle
    -- with vanishing truncation, hence a boundary.
    set δ := cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 c
    have hδ : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R δ = 0 :=
      cubicalChainDifferential_lof_zero _ _ _
    have hdp : cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (p - 1) = 0 := by
      simp [p, (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_one_eq_zero]
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB
      (z := α - δ * (p - 1))
      (by rw [map_sub, hα, (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).leibniz (cubicalChainLof_mem _ _ _), hδ,
        hdp, zero_mul, mul_zero, smul_zero, add_zero, sub_zero])
      (by rw [map_sub, map_mul, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_lof_zero, hc, hTp, hh, sub_self])
    exact ⟨δ, w, hδ, by rw [hw, add_sub_cancel]⟩

end Resolution
section Circle

/-- **Brown's resolution for the circle.** For the complex unit circle, based at `1`, with its
`1`-cell attached along the counterclockwise loop `t ↦ exp(2πit)`, every cycle of the free module
of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R` whose augmentation vanishes is a boundary: the module is a
semi-free resolution of `R` over the chains `C_*(Ω_1 S¹; R)` on the Moore loops of the circle. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    {R : Type} [CommRing R] {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m u = 0)
    (hε : loopCellAugmentation Circle 1 R u = 0) :
    ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m v = u := by
  -- `MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom` takes the inverse of the path class of the loop.
  have hg : MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom (1 : Circle) Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop =
      (FundamentalGroup.fromPath (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk Circle.expLoop))⁻¹ := by
    rw [MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom_apply, Path.toPath_toMooreLoop]
  refine exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    (fun n ↦ inferInstance) ?_ ?_ hu hε
  · rw [hg, Subgroup.zpowers_inv, Circle.zpowers_fromPath_expLoop]
  · rw [hg, isOfFinOrder_inv_iff]
    exact Circle.not_isOfFinOrder_fromPath_expLoop

end Circle

end TauCeti
